ts":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CimdPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether, and on what terms, a "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that is a URL is resolved by fetching the document"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it names (T21.5, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document"},{"type":"text","text":"). # Why this is one nested"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"policy rather than nine fields Every field here is a term of a single decision — "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"do we","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — and none of them means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anything without ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::allow_http","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dynamic_registration"},{"type":"text","text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"domains or ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this tenant’s"}]},{"text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument [","type":"text"},{"code":"OidcPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes for ","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". # Every bound here is a security control","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::min_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::max_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row written by hand cannot lift them.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CimdPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"CimdPolicy","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/maxMetadataBytes":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The hard cap on how many bytes of a document are read, before it is parsed. Clamped to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"CIMD_MAX_METADATA_BYTES_CEILING","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"